chemas, generated fixtures, and public SDK types stay byte-consistent; A contract consumer can select a valid projection for list and health without invoking either command; Negative controls fail when runtime modes and published modes diverge; Documentation explains modes, field selectors, and compatibility semantics within existing token ceilings"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Let agents choose a valid bounded-read projection without a failed exploratory call"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Contract discovery becomes executable, token-efficient, and identical to runtime validation across transports"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"GitHub #1105 reproduced on the current release and the complete all-status lineage has no focused owner beyond the broad token-budget feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"pm contracts --command list and pm contracts --command health publish their exact supported projection modes and selector vocabulary, with CLI and MCP consumers reading the same SDK-owned declaration."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The global ladder claims full, compact, brief, summary, and counts; list rejects summary and counts, health rejects compact and counts, and command-scoped contracts do not disclose the valid set."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.24"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"read-output contracts"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-5t33or","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-24T15:08:27.572Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_